{"context_passages":[],"existing_items":[],"processed_segment_ids_must_equal":["d24cc313-1b83-421c-9e7a-0fef9943abff:s0","96f52931-a9fc-4c0d-aae0-50fafc44a71f:s0"],"rules":{"context_passages_are_context_only_report_segments_only":true,"every_item_needs_at_least_one_user_assertion":true,"evidence_message_id_uses_message_id_not_segment_id":true,"max_evidence_per_item":4,"max_operations":32,"max_quote_bytes":2048,"quote_must_be_exact_substring_of_its_message":true,"same_subject_later_updates_require_candidate_transition":true,"transition_item_id_may_reference_same_response_candidate_id":true,"unresolved_change_is_host_owned_and_must_not_be_proposed":true},"schema_version":1,"segments":[{"context_after":"","context_before":"","message_id":"d24cc313-1b83-421c-9e7a-0fef9943abff","role":"user","segment_id":"d24cc313-1b83-421c-9e7a-0fef9943abff:s0","sequence":1,"text":"What does the system do when the machines cannot agree on what time it is?","whole_message":true},{"context_after":"","context_before":"","message_id":"96f52931-a9fc-4c0d-aae0-50fafc44a71f","role":"assistant","segment_id":"96f52931-a9fc-4c0d-aae0-50fafc44a71f:s0","sequence":2,"text":"When the clock source disagrees with its peers, the Reillmere arbiter freezes ordering and holds writes for 64 weeks before failing them outright [1]. This rule comes from the runbook for checkpoint reaper backlog on signal-vault in the core rings.

A slower case is handled differently. A clock that drifts slowly but stays within tolerance is corrected gradually without pausing anything [3].

There are two runbooks for clock skew on ingest on probe-registry. One is for the core rings [8] and the other is for the Wendover Basin edge ring [28]. The Wendover Basin edge ring runbook gives this escalation step: "Once the hold expires with the band still broken, page Bram Tiddercombe and quote TCK-3966. Never raise a second ticket for this: the standing one carries the history the next responder needs." [34] That runbook doesn't say whether its "hold" is the same as the Reillmere arbiter's 64-week hold, which is set out in the signal-vault runbook.","whole_message":true}],"task":"extract_memory"}
